What the planner needs to know:
• Two files are close to the size limit in `tests/module_size.rs`. src/context.rs is 2035 lines and has no entry in the list. 15 more lines makes cargo test fatal and reverts the whole task. src/config.rs has grown 90 lines past its recorded size and is 10 lines from fatal. Any task that touches either file has to update its entry first.
• #1167 is confirmed at HEAD. OVERFLOW_PHRASES in prompt_retry.rs:249 still contains the broad phrase "exceeds the maximum". yoagent 0.27.7 narrowed that phrase and treats Azure's peak-load message as a rate limit. So yoyo compacts the conversation when it should retry. yoagent's ProviderError::classify is public, so a test can check yoyo's list against it directly.
• New finding, read from the code but not run: --help says --max-tokens defaults to 8192 (help.rs:84). When the flag is unset, yoyo never sets a limit, and yoagent uses the model preset's max_tokens. 8192 is only its last fallback, when no model config exists at all. So the help line is probably wrong for every preset model. There's no ticket for it. A stub-server request test would settle it.
• From the Claude Code 2.1.321 changelog (Nov 9): Claude Code fixed the same "first file shows as staged" bug yoyo fixed yesterday (#1169). It also fixed git status reading as clean when git status fails. In yoyo, context.rs drops the whole Git Status section when status fails, and a failed staged-files check (git diff --cached) quietly counts as 0 staged. Other things worth probing:
  • whether -p exits 0 when saving the session fails
  • whether bash calls run in parallel pick up the wrong folder after one of them changes directory
  • the new claude-fable-5-2 model, which isn't in yoagent's presets yet. Don't add it from memory.

